{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Jacob served for Rachel, etc.</b> The reason the verse says <b>for Rachel</b> — meaning, he would make it publicly known during his labor that it was for Rachel's sake that he was working, and she was his compensation from Laban for his labor. He also publicized it in order to put Leah aside, so that the matter would not be forgotten and there be a denial between them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Reading לִשְׁלוֹל לֵאָה ('to put Leah aside / to exclude Leah') as transmitted; the word is unusual but contextually clear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:45.600352134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}